 "description": "Dose-response figure from 1928 (Percentage Positive Reactions vs Milliampere-minutes), a black-and-white scan, 2800x3600 PNG (the whole figure as supplied by tester feedback). Heavy black hand-ruled grid every 20 mA-min (X 140-240; the frame at 140 and 240) and every 20 % (Y 0-120; the frame at 0 and 120, labels to 100 only), all the same black as the series: one solid fitted curve, two dashed confidence curves whose hand-drawn dashes vary in length and gap (about 25-60 px dashes, 9-24 px gaps, 12-14 px strokes), hand-drawn 'x' and open 'o' / crossed-circle data markers on and beside the curves, several on gridline crossings. Hand-lettered tick labels at every 10 units, no tick marks. Hand-labelled by pixel analysis (NumPy/Pillow): positions are image pixels, origin top-left, integer = pixel centre. Gridline centres +/- 1 px (the lines are hand-ruled, uneven by up to +/- 5 px along their length; the left frame tilts from col ~311 at the top to ~319 at the bottom); the labelled values between gridlines are interpolated. Curve centrelines: the alpha-weighted centre of the curve's own run in every column where it stands clear of the gridline bands (+/- 10 px) and of markers, binned to a vertex every 20 columns (median), +/- 1 px; across gridline crossings and dash gaps the polyline interpolates. The fitted curve ends where it enters the end markers' rings (crossed circle at 150 / 25 %, circle at 225 / 100 %). Provenance and licence: fixtures/real/PROVENANCE.md.",
